WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:08.390
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:14.890
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.730
It's my day!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.310
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.710
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:42.090
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.490
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.270
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:02.410
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:09.910
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.050
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.120
I just want to walk

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.660
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.630
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:35.540
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:41.980
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.250
It's my day!

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.490
Ugh! Look at this place!
What a dump!

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.230
Is this it?

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.660
This is where we're going to live?

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.700
We haven't got a choice!

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.900
Your dad was fired
when his company had layoffs.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.910
They wouldn't let us stay
in the company housing...

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.770
...and we can't afford
anything better!

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.780
Well... there's still 
no place like home...

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.450
But, Tsukushi...
No matter what happens...

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.580
...I won't let you quit
Eitoku Academy.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:27.020
Our future depends
on you marrying somebody rich!

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.860
C-come on...

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.450
<i>Marry somebody rich?</i>

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:59.390
<i>I hurt Domyoji, and I couldn't win
Rui Hanazawa's heart...</i>

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.150
<i>There's just no way...</i>

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.730
Tsukasa...
You're really going to New York?

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.870
Will you be all right?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.070
How can anyone who can't
speak English hope to survive there?

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.240
You dope! That's the point!

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.510
But... you're coming
right back, aren't you?

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.880
Nope! I'm not coming back
for two years.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:32.360
Two years?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.620
<i>Domyoji's going to New York
for two years?!</i>

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.890
I'm leaving in three days.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.030
Tsukasa...

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.200
Rui... I'm not doing this
because of you.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:11.930
"Domyoji Goes to New York!!"

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:22.770
Why?!

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.410
Why are you leaving?

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.500
Makino...

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.380
You're just running off because you couldn't 
get Rui Hanazawa and me expelled!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.010
Way to go, Makino! Give him hell!

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:38.680
Yeah!

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.680
You... You...

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.590
Sorry to say this, Makino...

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.970
I'm not running away.
I'm going because I want to.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.630
This has nothing to do with you.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.100
Of course!
What could I have been thinking?

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:03.510
I'll feel a lot better when
you're gone.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.680
Go off to America, or Africa...
Wherever you like!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.180
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.370
<i>He's right... It has nothing
to do with me.</i>

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.280
What's the matter, Susumu?
Hurry up and eat!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:44.440
Huh? Is this all for dinner?
I can't survive on this.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.710
Don't complain!
This is the best we could do.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:52.790
When I find a new job,
we'll be able to live like before.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.720
But, if Tsukushi finds herself
a rich husband

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.160
all our problems will be solved.
Right, Tsukushi?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.000
Wha?

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.370
<i>There's such hope in their eyes...</i>

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.420
Are you sure about this, Tsukasa?

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.450
If you move in
with Mom and Dad there,

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.890
there's no telling when you'll be able
to return to Japan.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.130
I don't care.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.430
Tsukasa!

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.510
Sis...

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:59.120
Do you remember when I took
the teddy bear Rui loved so much?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.850
Huh? Oh, the one made
in England?

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.390
<i>Come on, Rui! Give it to me.</i>

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.060
<i>No!</i>

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.790
<i>Wait... Hey!</i>

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.560
Dad would have bought me one
if I'd asked,

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.530
but I wanted Rui's.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.590
<i>Give it to me! Come on! I want it!</i>

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.590
<i>No! I won't give it to you!</i>

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.010
The more Rui refused,
the more I wanted it.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.710
<i>No! You can't have it!</i>

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:39.440
I knew I'd done something awful,
but I just couldn't apologize.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.060
<i>It's your fault!
You should have let go.</i>

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:48.160
I figured he'd never forgive me,
but the next day...

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.370
<i>Good morning, Tsukasa...</i>

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.900
I thought I'd never be
the man he was.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.770
He probably doesn't remember it,
but someday,

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.980
I've got to make up
for what I did.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:02.840
Tsukasa...

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.350
You're not talking
about Tsukushi, are you?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.680
Is that why
you're going to New York?

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:14.720
No. I'd made up my mind.
Even before the basketball game.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.280
I'd decided, win or lose,
to go to New York to study.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.060
<i>Tsukasa...</i>

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:42.680
<i>I've got to find a few part-time jobs
to help the family.</i>

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.690
<i>Work and earn money...</i>

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.320
<i>I shouldn't think
about anything else right now!</i>

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:49.320
<i>Yes!</i>

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:59.400
<i>I never thought Domyoji
would go so far away.</i>

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:04.940
<i>I thought I'd always see him
somewhere on campus.</i>

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:09.940
<i>And we'd yell at each other...
I thought that would go on forever.</i>

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.510
Is this what you want?

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:13.250
Huh?

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.120
<i>Rui Hanazawa!</i>

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:25.720
It doesn't matter what I want.
I have no right to stop him.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.130
Oh?

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.100
When Shizuka left for Paris,
you gave me a whole lecture.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.430
Lecture?!

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:41.470
Anyway, the situation is different.
I don't feel anything for Domyoji.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:42.770
If that's the case...

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:45.210
Oh, yeah...

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:48.980
Lend me that thing.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:51.780
What thing?

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:22.180
Rui!

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.040
Tsukasa says it's not, but...

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.730
You and Makino are definitely
the reason he's going to New York.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:38.860
That's right.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:41.130
Me and Makino?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:45.560
Don't play dumb! You spent a night
together at his house, didn't you?

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:47.300
Yeah.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.640
What do you mean, "Yeah"?

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:51.870
A guy and a girl,
alone in a locked room...

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.580
You know what's going to happen.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:56.610
Tsukushi...

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:57.950
Hanazawa...

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:09.790
You're much more delicate
than I imagined.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.490
Please, you're embarrassing me...

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.470
I will always protect you.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:19.740
How's that?

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.770
Nothing happened.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.610
Nothing...

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.340
...happened?

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:35.620
She's tempting... A great woman...

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.700
I could get serious about her.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:58.840
That night, I considered
taking her to bed with me.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.930
<i>It's okay with me.</i>

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.830
Rui... You...

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.460
You're still not over Shizuka?

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.430
That's part of it...

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.140
But I do have to try to forget her.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.880
So what else is there?

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.790
I just can't betray Tsukasa.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:55.660
He and I have been friends
for 13 years. Since we were kids.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.430
I see. So that's how it stands.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.070
You're going to wait until Tsukasa
is completely over her...

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:09.370
But if you tell him that,
he'll turn cartwheels with joy.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:14.170
But I won't tell him yet.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:16.580
Why not?

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:25.960
Because a long time ago...
he tore my favorite teddy bear.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.230
What?

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.410
<i>Help Wanted...</i>

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:46.410
<i>Waitress; 950 yen/hour;
high school students welcome.</i>

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.480
<i>The pay is less than I'd hoped...</i>

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.360
<i>I may as well work longer hours
where I am now.</i>

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:10.400
<i>Domyoji... He's leaving tomorrow...</i>

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:14.770
<i>Is this what you want?</i>

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.270
<i>I'm not running away.
I'm going because I want to.</i>

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.780
<i>This has nothing to do with you.</i>

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:29.850
<i>That's right. This has nothing
to do with me now.</i>

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.100
Take care, Tsukasa.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:49.770
Yeah...

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.780
When you come back,
you'll be talking our ears off in English.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:55.810
Tsukasa...

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:58.750
Isn't this the first time
you're going to be separated from them?

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.420
That's right.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:02.750
Hey!

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.660
I'm so glad I made it.

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.830
Huh? Why are you here?

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:17.970
What?!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:23.340
But, I'm a member
of the F4, aren't I?

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.810
Did we say that?

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:27.740
Ya got me...

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.410
Hey, come on, you guys...

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:34.380
Tsukasa...
Did you tell Tsukushi good-bye?

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:37.850
If she wanted me to,
she'd have come.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:42.060
Yeah. Makino didn't come
to see you off, did she?

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.120
Tsukushi's in no position to do that.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.430
Her dad was fired
when his company had layoffs.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.500
She's desperately looking
for part-time jobs.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:52.830
Layoffs?

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.570
Aw! Penniless Tsukushi
is in a pinch.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:59.000
She's really having a tough time.
Poor thing...

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:04.010
Did her father work at the zoo?

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:10.280
Squirrel & Tiger

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:15.020
<i>Flight 006 bound for New York
is now boarding.</i>

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:17.520
<i>Please proceed to Gate 82.</i>

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:22.360
Well, it's time...

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:23.290
Yeah.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.770
Wait. Let me take some pictures.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.110
Good luck, now!

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.680
If you run into any
pretty blondes, go for it.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:07.370
Tsukasa!

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.350
A farewell gift from Makino.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.500
See you!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:48.610
<i>Domyoji... I guess he's gone by now.</i>

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.170
<i>A farewell gift from Makino.</i>

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.150
<i>Nothing happened between
Makino and me.</i>

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.910
Let me off! Stop the plane!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.920
Sir! Please calm down!

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:32.390
Shut up! I'm Tsukasa Domyoji!

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:36.360
Makino

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>I'm late...</i>

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:46.940
<i>I mustn't look so gloomy!
I've got to cheer up!</i>

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:49.740
I'm home!

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.750
W-what happened?
Did a burglar get in?

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:07.420
Dad!

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.360
Mom!

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.160
Susumu!

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.160
Dad... Dad...

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.060
He borrowed a million yen
from some loan sharks

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.510
and lost everything
at the horse races!

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:22.770
Loan sharks?

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:26.670
I was sure I would win.
I was sure.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.310
Then we wouldn't have to worry
about living expenses...

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.640
We're getting a divorce, dear.

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.380
Mom...

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.610
Mother!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.950
I can't stand
to live like this anymore!

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:41.790
In a place like this
and a million yen in debt?!

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.990
Wait a minute, Mom... Don't be hasty!

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:51.000
I don't like this either.
But we're family. The four of us!

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:55.530
Then what should we do?!
If we continue like this...

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:58.540
...our only choice is
to kill ourselves!

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:10.980
You're useless, dear!

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:17.220
<i>If he were here, he'd probably
say something really sarcastic.</i>

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.460
<i>Penniless Tsukushi...</i>

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.690
<i>You've finally reached
the bottom of the barrel.</i>

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:41.410
Makino residence...

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:45.310
<i>Tsukushi! Thanks to you,
I'm in an awful jam!</i>

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.850
Tsukasa?!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.320
<i>Come and get me in Vancouver.</i>

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:54.320
Vancouver... Isn't that in Canada?
Aren't you in New York?

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:57.990
<i>Never mind where I am!
Just come and get me.</i>

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.000
Hey! What's your answer?

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:04.970
Are you listening, Makino?

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.670
Why should I?!

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:11.510
My dad's a million in debt
and our family's about to fall apart!

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.180
Ask someone else, will you?

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.620
If you come and get me,
I'll lend you that million yen.

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:39.210
Tsk!

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.410
<i>Hey, Makino! Are you listening?</i>

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:54.650
Domyoji...

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:10.930
You let your hair down a little

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:18.800
You hid the fact
that you were crying

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:28.680
I noticed, but I
couldn't ask you why

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:36.720
I can never be
honest about how I feel

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:44.500
Until after we've split
up after a bad fight

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:52.640
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:52.640
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:22:52.640 --> 00:23:01.010
I can say "I love you"...

00:22:52.640 --> 00:23:01.010
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:10.790
Do you really hate me this time?

00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:18.560
Will you end up running to him?

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:26.740
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:26.740
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:35.150
I can say "I love you"...

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:35.150
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:49.730
What's going on?

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:53.600
What's Tsukasa doing in Canada,
when he should be in New York?

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:55.930
And he has the nerve
to tell me to come get him!

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:59.800
I'm a little embarrassed
about taking his million-yen bait.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:02.540
But Yuki's with me.
I've got to have some fun.

00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:06.240
Hana Yori Dango:
"Tsukushi Goes to Canada!!"

00:24:06.910 --> 00:24:07.910
The future looks bleak.
